{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPM-058", "label": "Study family SF-APPM-058: PNR shot-level season rates vs possession labels", "score": 0.439, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPM-058 (0.23)", "request matches RQC:RQC-048 (0.29); FAM:SF-APPM-058 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-048"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "PNR shot-level season rates vs possession labels", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "PBP-derived shot-level PNR rates sit in a realistic band (script notes possession-level rates will be higher) and vary by team as expected.", "observed_result": "2024-25 shot-level PNR share of half-court shots ranges from OKC 7.567% (498/6581) and BOS 7.854% to IND 13.824% (856/6192) and NYK 11.959%. ATL 11.361%, DEN 11.404%, PHX 10.232% (bh 7.050 / roll 3.181).", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "No pass/fail gate in the output; rates are a calibration input for PBPProxyPNR (later logs show calibrated PNR ~17.9-19.6% of possessions).", "observed_sample_and_power": "30 teams, half_court_shots ~5994-6581", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "descriptive", "observed_failure_type": "E_unclear"}, "relationships": []}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-009", "label": "Study family SF-CHT-009: Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type", "score": 0.406, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-CHT-009 (0.23)", "request matches RQC:RQC-055 (0.23); FAM:SF-CHT-009 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-055"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "Named star initiators have identifiable lineup and forced-play-type suppressors in the possession graph.", "observed_result": "Jokic vs MIN lineup PPP 0.814, -0.385 (n=59); Curry vs HOU 0.851, -0.358 (n=47); Doncic vs LAC 0.733, -0.396 (n=30); Giannis forced PULL_UP 0.848, -0.540 vs preferred DRIVE (largest gap).", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "No placebo or matching; later sequence work treated similar star-chain gaps as artifacts.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n>=30 for lineup cells cited", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_method": "Jokic/Curry/Doncic/Giannis; min-15 gate on 8 play types; opposing DEFENSE_LINEUP ~84% coverage; 272-row CSV."}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-067", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-067: TOV_FORCE 3-ply adversarial surviving lift", "score": 0.351, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-032 (0.37); FAM:SF-APPA-067 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-032", "FAM:SF-APPA-010 auto_related_family (record_link_related_to) FAM:SF-APPA-067"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "TOV_FORCE 3-ply adversarial surviving lift", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "Raw R1 TOV-force channel lifts survive opponent re-route or PT-shift (R2) and our follow-the-ball counter (R3).", "observed_result": "R1 lifts shrink ~50%+: ORL Banchero/Huerter +8.4 to net +3.7pp; DET Green/Anthony +7.0 to +3.5; PHI Harris/Vucevic +12.0 to +6.0; BOS Holiday/Council +6.1 to +2.8; PHX Booker/Wiggins +14.8 to +7.5; OKC Dort/Coffey +12.0  [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Net lift is model-implied, not observed in the games; R3 often additive surrogate at n<10.", "observed_sample_and_power": "4 games; 8 offense-defense sides", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "descriptive"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-010"}, {"rel": "auto_measures", "node": "VAR:turnovers"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-012", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-012: Defensive PPP allowed and possession share, RS vs playoffs", "score": 0.237, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-049 (0.33); FAM:SF-APPS-012 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-049", "request matches DS:Play_type_initiation_records_Neo4j_INITIATED_edges_play_type_possessions (0.17); FAM:SF-APPS-012 auto_uses_dataset DS:Play_type_initiation_records_Neo4j_INITIATED_edges_play_type_possessions"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Defensive PPP allowed and possession share, RS vs playoffs", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "Playoff defenses suppress DRIVE more than RS defenses (both lower PPP allowed and lower share).", "observed_result": "DRIVE allowed 1.191 -> 0.923 (-0.268), share 21.2% -> 18.2%; PNR -0.139, share +12.1pp; PULL_UP +0.341, share -7.6pp.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "No inferential test; PNR share jump of +12.1pp may reflect tagging differences.", "observed_sample_and_power": "25 teams", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_method": "25 defensive teams, min 30 poss per cell; RS vs playoff PPP allowed and opponent possession share by PT.", "observed_verdict": "descriptive", "observed_failure_type": "E_unclear"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:LABEL_ERROR"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR"}]}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).
